# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# OPEN CONFIG
# Real values, safe to commit. Loaded via Bun's native process.env (this is
# a tooling script, not a SvelteKit app, so there's no $env module here).
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=8582954a9e4c6f0259c6236be794d7d3

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SECRETS
# Left blank here; real values live only in .env.local (gitignored).
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Create as an account token (Manage Account -> API Tokens, not My Profile -> API Tokens), named
# "R2 - tools/r2 apply", with the account-scoped Account > Workers R2 Storage > Edit permission --
# like AI Gateway and D1, R2 doesn't expose a narrower per-bucket scope than that. Used by
# apply.ts, which shells out to `wrangler` -- wrangler reads this env var itself, same as
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID above.
#
# In practice, tools/databases's existing CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN (see tools/databases/.env.local)
# already has this scope and was reused here rather than minting a separate one -- confirmed
# working (2026-09-22): unlike tools/workers' Workers Builds API (see that package's .env), R2's
# admin API does accept Account-Owned tokens. That run only exercised the read/reconcile path
# (`bucket info`, `dev-url get`, `domain list`), since every declared bucket already matched
# config.ts -- the write path (`create`, `dev-url enable`, `domain add`) hasn't been exercised
# against this token yet.
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=
